%I A400355 #37 Nov 08 2026 14:08:36
%S A400355 1,6,24,90,336,1246,4592,16866,61840,226534,829512,3037242,11122272,
%T A400355 40740030,149278688,547197122,2006646624,7361806918,27020011640,
%U A400355 99213917082,364453522224,1339336023966,4923902141904,18109061567650,66625909706096,245213846545446
%N A400355 First column of the derivative-compositional Riordan array psi_2(f) = (f^[2](x)*(f^[2])'(x)/x, f^[2](x)), where f^[2](x) = f(f(x)), f(x) = x*s(x), and s(x) is the g.f. of A004148 (RNA secondary structures).
%C A400355 a(n) is the number of ordered pairs (W_0, W_1) of peakless lattice walks in which each E step receives one of 2 colors, of total length n, together with a distinguished gap in W_0.
%C A400355 For k >= 1, the derivative-compositional array is psi_k(f) = (f^[k](x)*(f^[k])'(x)/x, f^[k](x)), where f^[k] denotes the k-fold compositional iterate f o f o ... o f (not the k-th derivative). This sequence is column 0 of psi_2(f) for f(x) = x*s(x); here (f^[2](x)/x, f^[2](x)) is the square of the RNA I Riordan array (s(x), x*s(x)). The case k = 1 is A399173.
%D A400355 A. Nkwanta, Lattice paths and RNA secondary structures, DIMACS Series in Discrete Mathematics and Theoretical Computer Science, Vol. 34 (1997), 137-147.
%D A400355 L. W. Shapiro, S. Getu, W.-J. Woan, and L. C. Woodson, The Riordan group, Discrete Applied Mathematics, Vol. 34 (1991), 229-239.
%H A400355 Ifeyinwa Madu, <a href="/A400355/b400355.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..50</a>
%F A400355 G.f.: A(x) = f^[2](x)*(f^[2])'(x)/x = (1/(2*x)) * d/dx (x*g(x))^2, where g(x) = f^[2](x)/x = 1 + 2*x + 4*x^2 + 10*x^3 + 28*x^4 + ... is the g.f. of A187256 and satisfies (1 - 2*x + x^2)*g(x) = 1 + x^2*g(x)^2; i.e., g(x) = (1 - 2*x + x^2 - sqrt((1 - 2*x + x^2)^2 - 4*x^2))/(2*x^2).
%F A400355 a(n) = ((n+2)/2) * [x^n] g(x)^2.
%F A400355 a(n) = Sum_{j=0..n} (j+1)*b(j)*b(n-j), where b(j) = [x^j] g(x) = A187256(j).
%F A400355 a(n) = (n+2) * Sum_{p=0..floor((n-1)/2)} 2^(n-2*p)*binomial(n-p-1,p)*binomial(n-p+1,n-2*p-1)/(n-2*p) for n >= 1.
%F A400355 a(n) ~ c * (2+sqrt(3))^n / sqrt(n), where c = (26+15*sqrt(3))*sqrt(14*sqrt(3)-24)/(2*sqrt(Pi)) = 7.312829...
%F A400355 a(n) == 0 (mod 2) for n >= 1 (swapping the 2 colors of all E steps is a fixed-point-free involution).
%e A400355 With b(0..3) = 1, 2, 4, 10: a(3) = 1*b(0)*b(3) + 2*b(1)*b(2) + 3*b(2)*b(1) + 4*b(3)*b(0) = 10 + 16 + 24 + 40 = 90.
%o A400355 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 1, (n+2)*sum(p=0, (n-1)\2, 2^(n-2*p)*binomial(n-p-1,p)*binomial(n-p+1,n-2*p-1)/(n-2*p)));
%Y A400355 Cf. A004148, A187256, A399173.
%K A400355 nonn,easy,new
%O A400355 0,2
%A A400355 _Ifeyinwa Madu_, Oct 30 2026
